  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Decreasing order towards <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>1</mn></math> reaction for the following compounds is:</p><p><img src=\"assets\\qt0049_2e616636d64e.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 263px;\" />&nbsp;</p>"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "a &gt; c &gt; d &gt; b",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "a &gt; b &gt; c &gt; d",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "b &gt; d &gt; c &gt; a",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "d &gt; b &gt; c &gt; a",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The relative reactivity of alkyl halides in the&nbsp;S<sub>N</sub>1 reaction depends&nbsp;on the stability of carbocation. Electron-withdrawing groups decrease the stability and electron-releasing groups increase the stability of carbocations.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;group is an electron-withdrawing group by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>OMe</mi></math>&nbsp;is electron-releasing groups by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></math>&nbsp;effect. Hence, the overall order is&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0049_c6a0fb74c0f1.png\" style=\"width: 500px; height: 241px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>&nbsp;Reactivity order (b) &gt; (d) &gt; (c) &gt; (a)</p>"
  }
}